From 6b93d2730fc9df856613f85d4ca5f5e65d17d72d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:06:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs(skills): inline wiki links create links_to
 relations, not references

The memory-notes skill told readers that a wiki link in prose creates a
`references` relation. The parser (entity_parser.py, plugins.py) and
NOTE-FORMAT.md both use `links_to`, and the `#bm:links_to` directive is
named after it. Align the skill so agents filtering or writing relation
types use the label that is actually indexed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 skills/memory-notes/SKILL.md | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/skills/memory-notes/SKILL.md b/skills/memory-notes/SKILL.md
index b0c3ce3..68f25b4 100644
--- a/skills/memory-notes/SKILL.md
+++ b/skills/memory-notes/SKILL.md
@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@ the team has more experience with REST. See [[API Specification]]
 for the full contract.
 ```
 
-These create `references` relations automatically. Use the Relations section for explicit, typed relationships; use inline links for natural prose references.
+These create `links_to` relations automatically. Use the Relations section for explicit, typed relationships; use inline links for natural prose references.
 
 ### Relation Tips
 
